Z||000000||wro200||10-20-2001||11:03 PM||||my ck engine and oil psi lights come on when i shut the key off||||reg||5
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-21-2001||12:33 AM||||Wow, that's a stange one. Never heard of something like that happening. <BR>What year/trim level is it?<BR>Engine & tranny?<BR>Mileage?<P>I would start with unplugging the negative terminal on the battery for at least 15 seconds (I usually wait 1 min.) to clear the codes and start fresh. <BR>Caution: The car will run very lousy for a few minutes till the computer starts pulling the reigns in on some sensors!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Keep us informed...<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||10-21-2001||08:07 AM||||If I had to guess I would check the switch in column behind the lock cylinder. It probably thinks it's in the "on" position. <BR>Check it like this. before you get to you off position and the lights are off, wait a little bit. Just for the fuel pressure to drop a little. Then switch it to off and listen for your fuel pump to turn on. ||||reg||1
